ne points="9,12 21,12 " class="polyline" name="polyline" style="stroke: #2196f3; fill: none; stroke-width: 1px;"></polyline><polyline points="13,14 17,14 " class="polyline" name="polyline" style="stroke: #2196f3; fill: none; stroke-width: 1px;"></polyline><g points="15,5 15,10" class="polyline" name="pin" type="simple" netid="29" netidpos="0"><polyline points="15,5 15,10 " style="stroke: rgb(255, 0, 0); stroke-width: 1px;"></polyline><rect width="6" height="6" class="pin" x="12" y="2" style="stroke: rgb(0, 255, 0); fill: none; stroke-width: 1px; display: none;"></rect><text r="0" x="13" y="12" transform="rotate(90 13 12)" style="font-size: 12px; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; display: none;">p</text><text r="0" x="15" y="5" transform="rotate(0 15 5)" style="font-size: 12px; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; display: none;"> </text><ellipse cx="15" cy="8.5" rx="1.5" ry="1.5" style="stroke: rgb(255, 0, 0); fill: rgb(255, 0, 0); stroke-width: 1px; display: none;"></ellipse><polygon points="13.5,10 16.5,10 15,11.5 " style="stroke: rgb(255, 0, 0); fill: rgb(255, 0, 0); stroke-width: 1px; display: none;"></polygon></g><polyline points="7,10 23,10 " class="polyline" name="polyline" style="stroke: #2196f3; fill: none; stroke-width: 1px;"></polyline></g><text class="draggable" name="text" x="30" y="18" r="0" rtemp="0" transform="rotate(0 30 18)" style="fill: rgb(255, 123, 0); font-weight: normal; font-style: italic; font-size: 14px; font-family: lighter;">Logic gates with switches and LEDs (Live simulation)</text><text class="draggable" name="text" x="404" y="332" r="0" rtemp="0" transform="rotate(0 404 332)" style="fill: rgb(100, 116, 139); font-weight: normal; font-style: italic; font-size: 11px; font-family: lighter;">NOT</text><text class="draggable" name="text" x="404" y="432" r="0" rtemp="0" transform="rotate(0 404 432)" style="fill: rgb(100, 116, 139); font-weight: normal; font-style: italic; font-size: 11px; font-family: lighter;">OR</text><text class="draggable" name="text" x="404" y="532" r="0" rtemp="0" transform="rotate(0 404 532)" style="fill: rgb(100, 116, 139); font-weight: normal; font-style: italic; font-size: 11px; font-family: lighter;">NOR</text><text class="draggable" name="text" x="404" y="632" r="0" rtemp="0" transform="rotate(0 404 632)" style="fill: rgb(100, 116, 139); font-weight: normal; font-style: italic; font-size: 11px; font-family: lighter;">XOR</text><text class="draggable" name="text" x="404" y="732" r="0" rtemp="0" transform="rotate(0 404 732)" style="fill: rgb(100, 116, 139); font-weight: normal; font-style: italic; font-size: 11px; font-family: lighter;">XNOR</text><text class="draggable" name="text" x="326" y="48" r="0" rtemp="0" transform="rotate(0 326 48)" style="fill: rgb(100, 116, 139); font-weight: normal; font-style: italic; font-size: 11px; font-family: lighter;">A</text><text class="draggable" name="text" x="296" y="158" r="0" rtemp="0" transform="rotate(0 296 158)" style="fill: rgb(100, 116, 139); font-weight: normal; font-style: italic; font-size: 11px; font-family: lighter;">B</text><g transform="translate(720,20)" x="720" y="20" title="codeHTML" width="560" height="468" class="codeHTML" name="codeHTML" rot="0"><foreignObject x="0" y="0" width="560" height="468" style="width: 560px; height: 468px;"><div name="htmlCode" style="zoom: 0.56; height: 835.714px; width: 1000px;" code="&lt;div class=&quot;ch&quot;&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Logic Gates with Switches and LEDs (Live simulation)&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;ch-card&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;How to use&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open the &lt;strong&gt;Live Simulation&lt;/strong&gt; panel and press &lt;strong&gt;Run&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Click the two &lt;strong&gt;SPST switches&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;S1 (A)&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;S2 (B)&lt;/strong&gt;: closed = logic 1 (5 V), open = logic 0 (a 10 k&amp;Omega; pull-down resistor holds the input low).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Each gate drives a &lt;strong&gt;LED&lt;/strong&gt; (red, green, blue or yellow) through a 330 &amp;Omega; resistor: the triangle of the LED lights when the output is 1.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Circuit&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;V1:&lt;/strong&gt; 5 V supply, shared by all the switches through one wire.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;S1 and S2:&lt;/strong&gt; the inputs A and B. Each is an SPST switch between the supply and a wire that goes to the inputs of &lt;em&gt;all&lt;/em&gt; the gates (model SwitchSPST, parameter &lt;code&gt;state&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rp1 and Rp2:&lt;/strong&gt; 10 k&amp;Omega; pull-down resistors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Gates:&lt;/strong&gt; NOT (input A only), OR, NOR, XOR and XNOR (&lt;code&gt;Gates.py&lt;/code&gt;, digital models, logic family 0 V / 5 V).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rl and D:&lt;/strong&gt; 330 &amp;Omega; resistor and LED (symbols &lt;em&gt;LED Red / Green / Blue / Yellow&lt;/em&gt;, model &lt;code&gt;LED.py&lt;/code&gt;: the forward voltage Vf is 1.9 / 2.2 / 3.0 / 2.1 V). The triangle is a live segment bound to the parameter &lt;code&gt;lit&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Truth tables&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table style=&quot;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;padding:2px 10px&quot;&gt;A&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;padding:2px 10px&quot;&gt;B&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;padding:2px 10px&quot;&gt;OR&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;padding:2px 10px&quot;&gt;NOR&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;padding:2px 10px&quot;&gt;XOR&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;padding:2px 10px&quot;&gt;XNOR&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;center&quot;&gt;0&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;center&quot;&gt;0&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;center&quot;&gt;0&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;center&quot;&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;center&quot;&gt;0&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;center&quot;&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;center&quot;&gt;0&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;center&quot;&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;center&quot;&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;center&quot;&gt;0&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;center&quot;&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;center&quot;&gt;0&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;center&quot;&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;center&quot;&gt;0&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;center&quot;&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;center&quot;&gt;0&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;center&quot;&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;center&quot;&gt;0&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;center&quot;&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;center&quot;&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;center&quot;&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;center&quot;&gt;0&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;center&quot;&gt;0&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;center&quot;&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NOT: A = 0 gives 1 (LED on) and A = 1 gives 0 (LED off).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Things to try&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Close only A: the NOT LED goes off, OR and XOR light, NOR and XNOR are off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Close both A and B: XOR goes off and XNOR lights; OR stays on and NOR stays off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;With both switches open NOT, NOR and XNOR light (their output is 1 at input 00).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The LED current is about (4.3 V &amp;minus; Vf) / 330 &amp;Omega;, a few mA; the gate output resistance is 100 &amp;Omega;, so the output level is a little under 5 V while the LED is on. The blue LED (3 V) is the dimmest.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
